  "worked_solution": "An expression is a contradiction if it is always false, regardless of the inputs.\n\nBy completing the final column in the truth table below, we obtain the following:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,[(P∨Q)∧¬P]∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nAccording to the table, $[(P∨Q)∧¬P]∧¬Q$ \n$\\text{is}$\nalways false. Therefore, it \n$\\text{is}$\na contradiction.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
